{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers","id":672902,"title":"Supers hunting Slashers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-20T22:55:34-07:00","id":672902,"title":"Supers hunting Slashers","content":"First of all, I apologise if this should actually be on another board, this just seemed the best place to put it.<br /> <br /> Alright, we all know from other threads here that slashers can threaten other supernaturals, and that they can scare them. What I'm curious about is this: if other supernaturals took it into their heads to go hunting slashers, how well would they fare?<br /> <br /> Let's be honest: the general assumption of the World of Darkness is that open war doesn't erupt because every faction understands the principles of live and let live towards each other. As a whole, they try to avoid getting in each other's way, because the nights are hard and dangerous enough, yeah? But slashers don't get that. Slashers have never been very good at refraining from pissing in the soup, as the saying goes.<br /> <br /> They make waves. They're disruptive. They kill people - possibly people belonging to or cherished by the children of the night. They spawn angry ghosts, fuel spirits of murder/pain/bloodshed/fear, and generally pollute the spiritual landscape around them. They stir up the police and the media. They make life even harder for &quot;honest&quot; supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, there's a very poignant line in the Draugr entry in <i>Wicked Dead</i>, about how it's not often that vampires get to feel righteous, but hunting bestial Lust-driven draugr is one of those times. Well, there's something very similar in line when it comes to hunting down expies of Michael Myers, Freddy Krueger, Candyman, Leatherface and Jason Vorhees.<br /> <br /> So. The situation could be a Slasher has made a very poor choice in its next victims. Or it could be an analogue to that German film &quot;M&quot;, where the children of the night are banding together to destroy a Slasher who is making too many waves. Or it could be a NWoD Monster Mash take on that comic &quot;Hack Slash&quot;, about a group dedicated to hunting and killing Slashers. What skills can the various creatures of the night offer up to making hunting down and ending Slashers more plausible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T00:34:19-07:00","id":672965,"title":"","content":"Changelings can enter the dreams of a slasher. Sure, it is probably a risky maneuver, especially when dealing with masks, but it is a good way to gain valuable information on the slasher in question (its plans, motives, etc.). Some of the contracts are a good boon in tracking them down as well. For example, there are contracts that allow a Changeling to talk with objects and unless the slasher is aware of that fact, getting a good image of the slasher just by visiting a dump site is almost guaranteed. Whether or not their ability to travel the Hedge is a boon, depends a bit on the situation. The Hedge is a great tool to get out of Dodge, and it could help entering a hard to reach place (assuming the characters find a good path - not always easy). Come to think of it, Freddy Krueger sounds like a great opponent for a group of Changelings since it is all in a dream, although the Changelings are bound to be a bit sturdier than the poor victims in the movies since they are just as good in dream manipulation as Freddy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T01:16:41-07:00","id":672989,"title":"","content":"Yep. Super vs. Slasher is a very different thing from mortal vs. Slasher... although, admittedly, anything over tier 1 (and even then, depends on the Cell) is very different to &quot;innocents (as in, ignorant of the darker world) vs Slashers&quot; theme of the actual films that inspired them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, nice commentary on Changelings. Some input from me...<br /> <br /> To me, it seems like the two Supers most suited for fighting Slashers, and most focused <i>against</i> Slashers, are Werewolves and Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> Both races are not only clued into methods of tracking Slashers that far surpass human police agents, but they are actively receptive to the &quot;wakes&quot; Slashers make. It's very hard to ignore that a psycho killer has set herself up in your neighborhood when you are either constantly fighting the murder spirits she spawns/attracts or are being screamed at constantly by the vengeful ghosts of her victims. It's also pretty easy to find the evidence when you just have to A: ask the ghost of her victims, or B: look for the swarm of murder spirits.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters can attack Slashers from Twilight, either directly or by talking to the ghosts that the Slasher made. As Mortal Remains touches on, it's very, very hard for a loony killer to meaningfully assault a Sin-Eater, especially if he's leading the charge with angry ghosts.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are, to put it bluntly, murder machines. A pack of five or six raging Gauru will make mincemeat out of virtually anything they catch ahold of. Supernatural &quot;bruiser&quot; type Undertakings like the Mask can handle it a little better, but &quot;face&quot; types and most Scourges are pretty much kibble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T06:37:53-07:00","id":673115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers#post672902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, we all know from other threads here that slashers can threaten other supernaturals, and that they can scare them. What I'm curious about is this: if other supernaturals took it into their heads to go hunting slashers, how well would they fare?</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on the supernatural in question. A vampire could just mind control the guy. Dominate 1 means combat ends before it starts. Werewolves are used to hunting more dangerous prey than a Slasher. Mages would slaughter - few things can match a prepared mage, and if they're going hunting, they'll be prepared. Prometheans and sin-eaters laugh off damage. Changelings hunt through dreams and illusions. Mummies... hahahahahahhahaha. Demon? Yeah, starting character demonic embeds are more powerful than a highly experienced Slasher - and that doesn't include Demon Forms. Beasts would... make friends with the Slashers (hello automatic Good Impression), then possibly backstabbery.<br /> <br /> And all that isn't taking into account elders, alphas, masters, court rulers, founders, or cypher masters. Slashers are still humans - the upper bounds of their strength is still far below what a supernatural can achieve at high levels.<br /> <br /> Slashers are generally a bit stronger than hunters, and hunters can threaten supernaturals. However, hunters tend to be easy prey when the supernaturals start hunting them back. You need to be clever, resourceful, and in control to beat out a supernatural without any powers of your own. If the supernaturals are the ones being resourceful and in control, however? The shoe is on the other foot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's be honest: the general assumption of the World of Darkness is that open war doesn't erupt because every faction understands the principles of live and let live towards each other. As a whole, they try to avoid getting in each other's way, because the nights are hard and dangerous enough, yeah? But slashers don't get that. Slashers have never been very good at refraining from pissing in the soup, as the saying goes. </div> </div> </div> Most supernaturals don't go to war because they dont' know about each other (the Masquerade hides vamps from more than just humanity), and even if they did, they generally don't share any interests. Wars are fought over idealology and resources. Vampires, sin-eaters, and changelings don't deal with the Hisil, so why should a werewolf care about them? Demons are hyper focused on their war with God; why do they care about mummies collecting artifacts? Its not mutually assured destruction stopping a war, its apathy. With the exception of mages, hunters, and beasts, everyone is generally internally focused. And, even in the case of mages and beasts, they're more focused on studying/meeting the other supernaturals than any policing action. <br /> <br /> Nothing against why supers would go after a slasher, but the war reasons struck me as funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T06:45:58-07:00","id":673141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=673115#post673115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Depends on the supernatural in question. A vampire could just mind control the guy. Dominate 1 means combat ends before it starts. Werewolves are used to hunting more dangerous prey than a Slasher. Mages would slaughter - few things can match a prepared mage, and if they're going hunting, they'll be prepared. Prometheans and sin-eaters laugh off damage. Changelings hunt through dreams and illusions. Mummies... hahahahahahhahaha. Demon? Yeah, starting character demonic embeds are more powerful than a highly experienced Slasher - and that doesn't include Demon Forms. Beasts would... make friends with the Slashers (hello automatic Good Impression), then possibly backstabbery.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm getting here is that you should definitely go with a Mask if you want to put up a fight. <br /> <br /> That said, a while back I was in a Geist game where we ended up going against a charmer. Most of the challenge there was snapping out of his hold and starting the fight. He went down pretty quickly once we did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T07:31:28-07:00","id":673154,"title":"","content":"Most of the time, the Mask's defensive ability isn't that big of a deal. Its no defense against a vampire's mind control or a grapple/feed/choke. Werewolves are good with pack coordination to take and pin someone down, not just go on a claw-killing-spree. Mages have a whole host of better options than direct damage. Same with changelings. In 1e, rocket tag was a thing. Whomever got to strike first tended to dominate the fight. Mask ability just let them shrug off that first attack to make their own. Against a supernatural, however, there are too many ways to take someone down other than pure damage, even for dedicated combat characters.<br /> <br /> The hardest part of catching a Slasher is tracking them down. And Charmers / Geniuses are better at hiding than the other three, especially in plain sight. In a match of pure power, the supernaturals tend to come out on top, even against Scourges. That's true for hunters, and it remains true for slashers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T07:37:31-07:00","id":673156,"title":"","content":"On the other hand...<br /> <br /> &quot;I control his mind&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What mind?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T20:45:38-07:00","id":673825,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking most slashers don't stack up all that well against supernaturals. They can be a threat especially to weaker starting characters but as a supernatural grows in power and ability they can easily end up pulling a favorite stunt of the slashers themselves: making the hunter the hunted. A charmer kills a young man not knowing he was wolf blooded and gets torn to pieces by the boy's angry siblings. A mask finds himself thrown into one of the insanity driven realms of the fae touched after stalking some oddly acting teenagers at a summer camp. A legend stalks and murders a young women not realizing that he's killed the last human descendant a powerful vampire cared about and now the vamp has pulled a few strings and is bringing a few friends who know a thing or two about dealing with local legends. A vicious seductress lures a young man to a secluded area only to find out that everything is going as the mage planned and she's to be a very special sacrifice for the ritual that will keep him looking young.<br /> <br /> Now here's the fun part: There's nothing preventing a supernatural from acting or masquerading as a slasher. Imagine a group hunting down the killer in their area only to find out that instead of it being some weirdly empowered human with a jonesing for killing that it's one of their own kind and maybe they have powerful friends. Similarly you can twist things around and a group of players looking for what seems like a vampire is in reality a slasher with a similar MO. Heck maybe the slasher and the target they were after are working together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T01:16:33-07:00","id":673933,"title":"","content":"The real threat of most slashers against supernaturals is hardly physical. In fact, most slashers are going to die against a group of mortal Hunters in a direct confrontation. The problem is that slashers never fight fair. Sure, a vampire with Dominate can mind control a slasher, but first that vampire must realize what is going on and than track down the slasher. Granted, the slasher is at a similar disadvantage (unless he used to be a hunter), but I would place vampires among the easier targets of slashers. Their banes are too easy to abuse by a smart opponent, assuming the slasher even cares about actually killing the vampire in the first place. Most slashers apparently prefer to play with their favored police officer, or at least that is what the entertainment industry seems to think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of course, the real issue with slashers is in how to keep it fair to the players. If their car suddenly explodes because a genius wired it, they are rightfully going to complain. It might look a bit more sophisticated than rocks falling from the sky, but not by much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still, I am currently working on a slasher type story for my Changeling group. I am not aiming for the slasher to be a physically threatening opponent. Tracking him down is even going to be relatively easy. I am counting on a dream invasion, if not just that contract I talked about. The real pain is going to actually get into melee range. I just need to take care for it not to become too frustrating. I have never been a big fan of those reoccurring serial killers in all those detective series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T03:41:28-07:00","id":674022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=673825#post673825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now here's the fun part: There's nothing preventing a supernatural from acting or masquerading as a slasher.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Belial's Brood, Bale Hound, Scelesti, Flux Refinement follower, one of the Mad, a Reaper, or an extreme Sabatour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T06:09:26-07:00","id":674082,"title":"","content":"Supernaturals don't have to fear a Slasher's physicality or powers. That's not what it's about. Instead, it's the unpredictability that one must fear. Whether mage, werewolf, or vampire,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> After all, Batman has nothing to fear from the Joker in terms of his power, right?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T07:05:39-07:00","id":674147,"title":"","content":"If you want to up their power you can always have a murder or death or torture spirit Claim them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T10:21:57-07:00","id":674370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=674022#post674022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Belial's Brood, Bale Hound, Scelesti, Flux Refinement follower, one of the Mad, a Reaper, or an extreme Sabatour?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone from the 'primary' factions can have an incessant desire to kill people and follow through with it too. So Lancea et Sanctum, Iron Masters, Tin Refinement followers, Free Council, Advocates or Inquisitors. Or any of the other dozens of groups.<br /> <br /> It's part of the whole thing with the rippers. There's nothing supernatural about them, they are 'just' serial killers. And anyone can be a serial killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-22-2015, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:58:42-07:00","id":674661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=674370#post674370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone from the 'primary' factions can have an incessant desire to kill people and follow through with it too. So Lancea et Sanctum, Iron Masters, Tin Refinement followers, Free Council, Advocates or Inquisitors. Or any of the other dozens of groups.<br /> <br /> It's part of the whole thing with the rippers. There's nothing supernatural about them, they are 'just' serial killers. And anyone can be a serial killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. You don't have to be from one of the far out crazy factions to be a murder obsessed nutcase and that's what makes the super gone slasher so terrifying. Slashers are powerful compared to humans yes but most of them can't compare to the more powerful supernaturals in the WoD. One of the supers going slasher however is a different story and can present a much higher level of threat. Imagine that VASCU is tracking what they think is one of these seemingly amped up serial killers only for its agents to run into a powerful and deranged vampire or mage. They're already ill equipped to deal with the slashers they often face to say nothing of the more common things that go bump in the night in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T00:51:15-07:00","id":675012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=674661#post674661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much. You don't have to be from one of the far out crazy factions to be a murder obsessed nutcase and that's what makes the super gone slasher so terrifying. Slashers are powerful compared to humans yes but most of them can't compare to the more powerful supernaturals in the WoD. One of the supers going slasher however is a different story and can present a much higher level of threat. Imagine that VASCU is tracking what they think is one of these seemingly amped up serial killers only for its agents to run into a powerful and deranged vampire or mage. They're already ill equipped to deal with the slashers they often face to say nothing of the more common things that go bump in the night in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't the slasher book discusses this? I would dare say that most of the supernaturals drawing the attention of Hunter groups are serial- and/or mass murderers by the definition of the law. It is just that when VASCU realizes they are hunting something besides 'regular' slashers they call TF:V.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:43:02-07:00","id":675684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=675012#post675012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't the slasher book discusses this? I would dare say that most of the supernaturals drawing the attention of Hunter groups are serial- and/or mass murderers by the definition of the law. It is just that when VASCU realizes they are hunting something besides 'regular' slashers they call TF:V.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's assuming the VASCU agents survive uncompromised and even then most VASCU agents don't like TFV at all since the latter tends to barge in on cases, take them over, and kick VASCU to the curb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:35:20-07:00","id":675708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=674082#post674082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, Batman has nothing to fear from the Joker in terms of his power, right?</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering that both are human, and the latter is willing to use a gun? I'd say that's plenty to fear. The Joker is Batman's opposite. The Clown Prince against the Dark Knight. Light and happy against dark and brooding. They're actually on par when it comes to gadgets, and have traditionally been roughly a match when it comes to a fight. Well, at least to the point where there's an actual fight and not a one-sided slaughter. <br /> <br /> But then, this is equivalent to a hunter versus slasher fight. If we talk about Superman or Green Lanturn versus the Joker, that's another matter entirely. The Joker is smart enough to bring yellow or kryptonite to the fight, but without preparation, its a onesided slaughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T15:19:48-07:00","id":675740,"title":"","content":"I think it could turn out nicely.<br /> <br /> Vampires dealing with a Psycho or Legend who only kills during the daytime. Werewolves dealing with a territorial Mask or Mutant who uses a silver weapon. Mages with a Maniac who uses insane clues that run them around in circles while actually targeting people they may have cared about.<br /> <br /> You probably won't go far with just a random serial killer but if the Slasher, for whatever reason, enjoys targeting those supernaturals or just happens to take advantage of the supernatural's weakness you could have a pretty nice story with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T15:25:26-07:00","id":675743,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest problem slashers will face is that... against supernaturals, they aren't all that impressive.<br /> <br /> Against humans, their bag of tricks allows them to contend with groups, but groups of supernaturals can easily stockpile buffs and other such nonsense to negate any inherent abilities of the slasher quite trivially.<br /> <br /> No, Slashers cannot by themselves deal with a supernatural threat; they need other slashers or at least... henchmen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hm, with that in mind, anyone ever though of making little helpers for the existing slashers, like Wolfblooded for supernatural serial killers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T15:52:47-07:00","id":675753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=675743#post675743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Slashers cannot by themselves deal with a supernatural threat; they need other slashers or at least... henchmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that. Not every supernatural is a combat beast, and the primary supernaturals can be killed pretty easily if you have the right equipment or strike at the right time. For vampires, fire and daylight. There's an arsonist Slasher right in the book. For werewolves, silver. There's a Freak with a golden arm in the book. Mages are as human as everyone else and can be tricked or taken by surprise. And there's plenty of Slashers who use surprise. Not every Slasher is some brute that's just going to walk up to your characters and start attacking them. Just like not every supernatural is a newly awakened Mummy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hm, with that in mind, anyone ever though of making little helpers for the existing slashers, like Wolfblooded for supernatural serial killers. </div> </div> </div>The Maniac's undertaking can sort of lead to something like that. I've been working on a microtemplate to expand on an idea I read about in a book, the First Victim's Club. In the book, very rarely, a serial killer's first victim will be sort of reborn and act as if under a state of Vinculum towards their murderer.<br /> <br /> But if Slashers need help they can always reach out to the Hunt Club or their own Allies or the police.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T18:08:06-07:00","id":675866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=675708#post675708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Considering that both are human, and the latter is willing to use a gun? I'd say that's plenty to fear. The Joker is Batman's opposite. The Clown Prince against the Dark Knight. Light and happy against dark and brooding. They're actually on par when it comes to gadgets, and have traditionally been roughly a match when it comes to a fight. Well, at least to the point where there's an actual fight and not a one-sided slaughter.<br /> <br /> But then, this is equivalent to a hunter versus slasher fight. If we talk about Superman or Green Lanturn versus the Joker, that's another matter entirely. The Joker is smart enough to bring yellow or kryptonite to the fight, but without preparation, its a onesided slaughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman's a master of 147 fighting styles, knows magic, has defeated everyone from Superman to Darkseid, and is arguably one of the most powerful characters in comics. Which means he, theoretically, should mop the floor with the Joker.<br /> <br /> But he doesn't.<br /> <br /> Which was my point.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, I should've worded it better. They're also most definitely NOT &quot;on par&quot; when it comes to gadgets, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> A supernatural(Batman, in my argument) should have no trouble with a Slasher(The Joker, in my argument) in a straight up fight due to the overwhelming odds in Batman's favor, yet in comic book lore, he most certainly does. Similar to my comparison, the sheer insanity and unpredictability of a Slasher should allow him to more than enough hold his own in a fight against foes you would normally consider far more powerful.<br /> <br /> Joker has fought and held his own against many superpowered foes as well. Like I said, the unpredictable nature can go a long way. Even against a Green Lantern ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T18:49:21-07:00","id":675897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=675753#post675753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say that. Not every supernatural is a combat beast, and the primary supernaturals can be killed pretty easily if you have the right equipment or strike at the right time. For vampires, fire and daylight. There's an arsonist Slasher right in the book. For werewolves, silver. There's a Freak with a golden arm in the book. Mages are as human as everyone else and can be tricked or taken by surprise. And there's plenty of Slashers who use surprise. Not every Slasher is some brute that's just going to walk up to your characters and start attacking them. Just like not every supernatural is a newly awakened Mummy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Maniac's undertaking can sort of lead to something like that. I've been working on a microtemplate to expand on an idea I read about in a book, the First Victim's Club. In the book, very rarely, a serial killer's first victim will be sort of reborn and act as if under a state of Vinculum towards their murderer.<br /> <br /> But if Slashers need help they can always reach out to the Hunt Club or their own Allies or the police.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another good example of this is Johann from the anime/manga Monster. Just take his charisma and the orphans under his control and turn them toward more useful endeavors other than offing themselves for the lulz.<br /> <br /> Now as I said slashers can be dangerous to supers much in the way that hunters can be a danger to supers but similarly unless they seriously stack the deck against your average medium tier super (who will almost certainly have some fair build up of combat abilities just to survive the other things in the WoD) most slashers will be the underdog in that fight. So let's look at some of the aspects of their various prey (Let's also assume we're considering slashers that are actually looking to pick a fight with a super and are actually prepared): <br /> <br /> Vampires: They have some of the most obvious banes (Hell all it takes is a breath spray and a Bic to ruin a Kindred's night) but they have two traits that can make them major pains in the ass. The first is that vampires are the most likely of the supers to strike through proxies and this means that a slasher may have to contend with the likes of blood dolls, ghouls, and even possibly the vamp sending the police and/or VASCU after them. The good news here is that if a slasher is smart and can get the jump on them most of these proxies won't be too hard to handle unless they come heavily armed and armored and have large numbers to back themselves up (Hint: They rarely do). The nastier trait is the powers a vampire can bring to bare and the funny thing it's not the more obvious combat monster type powers a slasher has to worry about. Things like being able to command animals to attack, shapeshifting, mental domination, being able to seemingly blend into the shadows, and some of the other weirder powers can definitely present a problem unless the slasher can lure their prey to a special location that helps to deal with these abilities.<br /> <br /> Werewolves: Again they have a very obvious bane though a little more expensive to get than the makeshift flamethrower mentioned above. While they do have many rites, a few funky artifacts, and the ability to turn into giant snarling death machines, a werewolf's biggest threat comes from the fact that they are pack animals. Mess with one alone or not and the victim's packmates will be looking for answers and eventually revenge. This is where having a group of slashers can be very helpful (And if we're talking a freak or mutant cannibal clan with a taste for furry it means more meat on the table). Really for werewolves the best strategy is either take them out quickly from a distance (The ole' silver bullet) or trick them into a tight area with plenty of hiding places so their strength, speed, and numbers don't count for as much.<br /> <br /> Mages: They're pretty much human so surprise is what works best but that surprise better take them out. The more time a mage is given, the more likely they throw out something the slasher can't handle. The big issue with a mage is that it can be hard to figure out what they're capable of and plan accordingly. The social predator types of slashers can potentially have a leg up in this area by using their charms to disadvantage the victim prior to the attack.<br /> <br /> Changelings: The big problem here is that many of their powers are such that a slasher may have a very difficult time countering them. Again, surprise and efficient killing go a long way.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters: These guys can be a slasher's worst nightmare. Being able to communicate with prior victims' spirits can give them knowledge which can be used to predict and limit the slasher's options. There's also the thing about potentially helping said spirits be able to directly target the slasher. They're mostly human though so again surprise and kill quickly.<br /> <br /> Prometheans: The bic flamethrower works here too. The real problem isn't their abilities more often than not but rather the fact that they aren't obvious to casual inspection. A slasher can easily get into trouble by attacking what he thinks is a human but it turns out to be one of these things.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T19:31:27-07:00","id":675956,"title":"","content":"I think the only problem with the Batman vs Joker analogy is the way you're coming at it. And, really, the way we're all mentioning how slashers work.<br /> <br /> Joker doesn't hunt down Batman trying to kill him. He wants him to give up or give in. And as a Storyteller you're, generally, not trying to kill the PCs in your games, you're trying to make a story for them.<br /> <br /> A slasher, likewise, doesn't have to be targeting a PC. They don't have to throw down in the middle of a club. Slashers can be insidious threats. A PCs ghoul is a slasher, and ghouls of the PC's rivals start disappearing. The Saint Satan killer keeps displaying his victims over powerful loci, tainting them with the attention. A mage's proximus 'apprentice' runs off to meet the mother who abandoned them, only to fall into a trap and be beaten to death with a crowbar. The opportunity for Slashers in 'regular' supernatural games extends beyond a Street Fighter type fight scene. Killing or getting rid of the Slasher is one thing, dealing with the fallout of what they've done and how its affected the PCs is what can make good stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T20:19:33-07:00","id":675985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=675897#post675897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sin-Eaters: These guys can be a slasher's worst nightmare. Being able to communicate with prior victims' spirits can give them knowledge which can be used to predict and limit the slasher's options. There's also the thing about potentially helping said spirits be able to directly target the slasher. They're mostly human though so again surprise and kill quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, unless they are low on plasm, Sin-Eaters are hardly easy to take down, even with surprise. And unless their Geist doesn't like them or agrees not to raise them, killing them will just piss them off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=675956#post675956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A slasher, likewise, doesn't have to be targeting a PC. They don't have to throw down in the middle of a club. Slashers can be insidious threats. A PCs ghoul is a slasher, and ghouls of the PC's rivals start disappearing. The Saint Satan killer keeps displaying his victims over powerful loci, tainting them with the attention. A mage's proximus 'apprentice' runs off to meet the mother who abandoned them, only to fall into a trap and be beaten to death with a crowbar. The opportunity for Slashers in 'regular' supernatural games extends beyond a Street Fighter type fight scene. Killing or getting rid of the Slasher is one thing, dealing with the fallout of what they've done and how its affected the PCs is what can make good stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing ruins a good Cover quite like its key element getting offed by some addled psycho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-23-2015, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T01:28:51-07:00","id":676168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=675753#post675753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maniac's undertaking can sort of lead to something like that. I've been working on a microtemplate to expand on an idea I read about in a book, the First Victim's Club. In the book, very rarely, a serial killer's first victim will be sort of reborn and act as if under a state of Vinculum towards their murderer.<br /> <br /> But if Slashers need help they can always reach out to the Hunt Club or their own Allies or the police.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Genius/Lunatic undertakings actually include powers to create new slashers by talking with them for some extensive time. Those are the slashers from movies that use others to do the killing for them whether those others are people or machines/traps. One of the prime examples is somebody who got over a dozen of others to suicide/kill with no evidence he was ever truly involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:25:38-07:00","id":676797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=675866#post675866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman's a master of 147 fighting styles, knows magic, has defeated everyone from Superman to Darkseid, and is arguably one of the most powerful characters in comics. Which means he, theoretically, should mop the floor with the Joker.<br /> <br /> But he doesn't.<br /> <br /> Which was my point.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, I should've worded it better. They're also most definitely NOT &quot;on par&quot; when it comes to gadgets, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> A supernatural(Batman, in my argument) should have no trouble with a Slasher(The Joker, in my argument) in a straight up fight due to the overwhelming odds in Batman's favor, yet in comic book lore, he most certainly does. Similar to my comparison, the sheer insanity and unpredictability of a Slasher should allow him to more than enough hold his own in a fight against foes you would normally consider far more powerful.<br /> <br /> Joker has fought and held his own against many superpowered foes as well. Like I said, the unpredictable nature can go a long way. Even against a Green Lantern ring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the only reason Batman has been able to hold his own or even defeat beings like Superman or Darkseid is <i>shitty writing</i>. Batman is not a supernatural entity, he's a Hunter with lots of money and the writers on his side.<br /> <br /> And Joker should no more be able to go toe to toe with Superman than Batman should, it's just bad writing and inconsistent characterization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:14:50-07:00","id":676884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=676797#post676797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the only reason Batman has been able to hold his own or even defeat beings like Superman or Darkseid is <i>shitty writing</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever reason you think, he has done it.<br /> <br /> Though I'm curious, and lets face it you were wanted a reaction, since he's been handled by some of the best writers in the business, what makes you say it's such poor writing? The rare scene where he's defeated Darkseid or Superman certainly fit the context, just as much as those where he's been killed by Darkseid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:40:43-07:00","id":676900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=675985#post675985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, unless they are low on plasm, Sin-Eaters are hardly easy to take down, even with surprise. And unless their Geist doesn't like them or agrees not to raise them, killing them will just piss them off.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are limits to what plasm can do however. A sin-eater whose damage track is filled with negated damage can't spend anymore plasm for negation. They also won't be holding all of their plasm in reserve for healing blows (unless possibly if they're psyche 1) and plasm spending limits still apply. Given how quickly a slasher can rack up the damage with a series of frenzied attacks most of your average sin-eaters (psyche 1-5) are still going to struggle with keeping themselves going while still mounting any kind of successful offense. Either they have a hard time negating all of the damage of a given attack or they quickly run out of health boxes and have to take the full damage thereafter. Sin-eaters are tougher than normal humans but surprisingly they hit the limits of their resilience much faster than many other supers (This is balanced by them being able to easily negate incoming aggravated damage up to the normal limits of course).<br /> <br /> Finally there are limits to the resurrection capabilities of a geist. If the body is severely dismembered (or even simply decapitated), cremated, or eaten the geist won't bother to try bringing the sin-eater back. Since I was talking about a slasher that at least understands the prey they're targeting the slasher isn't going to leave the body in a condition to be brought back.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T17:24:03-07:00","id":677062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=676884#post676884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For whatever reason you think, he has done it.<br /> <br /> Though I'm curious, and lets face it you were wanted a reaction, since he's been handled by some of the best writers in the business, what makes you say it's such poor writing? The rare scene where he's defeated Darkseid or Superman certainly fit the context, just as much as those where he's been killed by Darkseid.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an avid comic reader, I have to say that the whole &quot;Bat-God&quot; phenomenon is getting old. The fact is, Batman struggles with local mob bosses in his own book, so how is it that in another heroes story, he can whup a guy that has been slowly killing the universe just by EXISTING!? Batman in his own comic is a Hunter. He would be head of his own Conspiracy, (and he was, for a little while; Batman Incorporated, I plan on stating that up someday) but still not supernatural. What he knows of magic is some basic hedge magic and how to throw a monkey (with or without the wrench) into other peoples rituals, he never does any casting of his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T17:50:20-07:00","id":677082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=677062#post677062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an avid comic reader, I have to say that the whole &quot;Bat-God&quot; phenomenon is getting old. The fact is, Batman struggles with local mob bosses in his own book, so how is it that in another heroes story, he can whup a guy that has been slowly killing the universe just by EXISTING!?</div> </div> </div> </div>He shot a dying Darkseid with a god-killing bullet of Darkseid's design and 'died,' while doing so. I don't think saying he 'whupped' the guy really explains what happened very well. I think the issue with the 'Bat God' concept is mostly overblown by folks who, for whatever reason, get upset at the idea of Batman doing these things. It started in Morrison's JLA arc, where Batman in a very ungodly manner, used the very well known weakness of fire against martians. While he was very much a tactical genius in other comics, he was also knocked into the JLA emergency room every other story arc. He also quite literally died, during a future timeline, at the beams of Darkseid. Darkseid and Batman do butt heads, mostly because Batman is the mortal version of Orion, destined to kill Darkseid, but he's lost every actual fight they've had where he wasn't backed up by superpowers.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://ifanboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/07/JLA14Pg19.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I bring it up because I see this complaint leveled a lot at Batman, when it is really a matter of comics being comics. Spider-man has defeated Galactus. Black Panther the Silver Surfer. Wolverine and Iron Man have both beaten Magneto. Wolverine even killed him. Twice. Havoc the Hulk. The list goes on throughout the history of comics, and the vast majority of them don't involve Batman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Batman in his own comic is a Hunter. He would be head of his own Conspiracy, (and he was, for a little while; Batman Incorporated, I plan on stating that up someday) but still not supernatural. What he knows of magic is some basic hedge magic and how to throw a monkey (with or without the wrench) into other peoples rituals, he never does any casting of his own. </div> </div> </div>I don't want to put words in Dude of Legend's mouth, but I think what he was trying to say is that due to his extreme level of ability, vast access to resources and contacts and allies, he is comparable to a supernatural splat, especially when confronting a non-supernatural threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-24-2015, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T18:10:57-07:00","id":677102,"title":"","content":"I am aware of the various upsets you speak of; these are all cases of the literary equivalent of &quot;ST fiat&quot;. They should not be taken as examples of how powerful Batman, Spider-Man, Black Panther, Wolverine, or Havoc &quot;truly&quot; are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T18:27:21-07:00","id":677114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=676168#post676168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Genius/Lunatic undertakings actually include powers to create new slashers by talking with them for some extensive time. Those are the slashers from movies that use others to do the killing for them whether those others are people or machines/traps. One of the prime examples is somebody who got over a dozen of others to suicide/kill with no evidence he was ever truly involved.</div> </div> </div> </div> Like Joker did with Harley Quinn. When I first read Slashers, I couldn't help but profile some of the Arkham inmates as various Undertakings:<br /> <br /> Riddler; Genius, he's obsessed with proving his intellectual superiority.<br /> Joker; Lunatic, Harley's not the only one he's driven off the deep end.<br /> Two-Face; Freak, I don't think I need to explain why\u200b.<br /> Killer Croc; Mutant, also pretty obvious.<br /> <br /> I'm having a harder time thinking of good examples of the other Undertakings right now, maybe I'll start a thread about it when I do...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T23:36:47-07:00","id":677365,"title":"","content":"One thing I don't think I've seen in this thread is hunters handing a slasher problem they can't handle to a supernatural splat. Say the slasher is a member of a nearby cell or compact, or even embedded in a conspiracy. Well, hunters killing hunters is a bad image to play up. But managing to get the problem taken care of by another group, with a promise of a favor or deal in the future if it's a particularly large problem we're talking about, I have to imagine there's a few other splats willing to take that bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T06:29:05-07:00","id":677557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=677365#post677365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I don't think I've seen in this thread is hunters handing a slasher problem they can't handle to a supernatural splat. Say the slasher is a member of a nearby cell or compact, or even embedded in a conspiracy. Well, hunters killing hunters is a bad image to play up. But managing to get the problem taken care of by another group, with a promise of a favor or deal in the future if it's a particularly large problem we're talking about, I have to imagine there's a few other splats willing to take that bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's been my experience that a lot of the forum don't like the idea of 'cancer cells,' which I think this might fit under, since it could compromise a hunter cell. I like the idea, though, especially since it's possible for hunters to have non-antagonistic ties to supernaturals, and not all hunters are about killing everything that is supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T07:37:52-07:00","id":677595,"title":"","content":"There is one good example from reality I think fits with this idea. In Northern Ireland there was a cell of the Ulster Volunteer Force that became known as the Shankhill Butchers, who were infamous for using the Troubles as an excuse to kill innocent people. Eventually the IRA managed to somehow kill their leader in the middle of a Loyalist stronghold, which has led to suspicion that either the UVF had Murphy killed due to his being a &quot;liability&quot;, or a rival Loyalist paramilitary had him killed to weaken the UVF. In that kind of context, the idea that a hunter cell would let someone else do the dirty work isn't so far out of reach in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 09-25-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T14:26:22-07:00","id":677996,"title":"","content":"My speculation:<br /> <br /> If the IRA or some other Republican group did it I'd say they hired a Changeling because of the obvious Ireland-faerie connection and because faeries make great assassins for hire. They're stealthy and if you write a water tight contract they're going to stick to it. If it was a Loyalist group I'd say it was just regular old hunters since it's much easier to do the deed when you don't need to sneak past a fortress of your enemies.<br /> <br /> Or the dark horse possibility. The Ascending Ones did it. They're stealthy enough to pull it off, and seeing themselves on the side of the innocent civilians is their usual MO.<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW. What Undertaking do you think the Shankhill Butchers would be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T20:03:35-07:00","id":678436,"title":"","content":"Oh, right, I've been away so long I forgot you were British.<br /> <br /> Well, in WoD, I don't think the Butchers would've actually been slashers. To me at least, there is some kind of line separating a serial killer or mass murderer from being a slasher, but for the sake of the thread I'd say Lenny Murphy and some of the Butchers were probably Brutes with the rest being your average human beings who were either in awe or fear of Murphy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T00:12:37-07:00","id":678602,"title":"","content":"To me that line is the ability to stop your killing. Lets say a gang kills your family and you vow revenge, what happens after you get the last member? If you go stop killing you're a regular mortal, if you are compelled to find new targets you're a Slasher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T11:31:08-07:00","id":679198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/672902-supers-hunting-slashers?p=677082#post677082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want to put words in Dude of Legend's mouth, but I think what he was trying to say is that due to his extreme level of ability, vast access to resources and contacts and allies, he is comparable to a supernatural splat, especially when confronting a non-supernatural threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I was trying to say. I probably could've worded it better, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}